{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7e1c9a0-4f2e-4c3a-9d1e-sprint7full001",
    "name": "Sprint 7 — Trade API + Fauxnance",
    "description": "Every real HTTP call in this sprint: trade-api (running at 10.8.78.168:8085) and the live Fauxnance sandbox. No collection variables — every value below is literal.\n\n**Read before running:**\n\n1. **Fauxnance's mock data is US-equity only.** The demo seed's own instruments (`TCS`, `INFY`) are NOT in it — every request here uses `AAPL` instead. If `AAPL` isn't in the `instruments` table on this environment yet, insert it first:\n```sql\nINSERT INTO instruments (isin, ticker, name, type, exchange, is_active, currency)\nVALUES ('US0378331005', 'AAPL', 'Apple Inc.', 'EQUITY', 'NASDAQ', TRUE, 'USD')\nON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;\n```\n2. **The two Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN> pre-minted, long-lived (~5 years) HS256 JWTs** signed with the dev secret `dev-only-change-me-this-secret-is-not-for-production-use` — one for account 1 (ACTIVE), one for account 2 (SUSPENDED, used only by the ACC-403 example). They only work if `JWT_SECRET`/`JWT_ISSUER` on 10.8.78.168 are still the `.env.example` defaults. If that server uses a different secret, every request will 401 and these need re-minting.\n3. **This file now contains a real Fauxnance API key and long-lived tokens in plain text.** Treat it as sensitive — don't commit it to a shared repo or hand it out beyond your team.\n4. **No auto-capture / no dynamic idempotency keys** (both were variable-dependent features, removed along with the variables). The 'Place Order' request's `idempotencyKey` is a fixed literal — re-running it a second time as-is will hit ORD-409; edit that field manually for a fresh order each time. Same for 'Cancel Order': paste in a real order UUID by hand, there's nothing to auto-fill it from.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Trade API",
      "description": "sprint-06-trade-api, http://10.8.78.168:8085. Every endpoint OrderController/AccountController expose, plus the actuator health check.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://10.8.78.168:8085/actuator/health",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": ["10", "8", "78", "168"],
              "port": "8085",
              "path": ["actuator", "health"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Place Order — fillable BUY (AAPL, limit above ask)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN>" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"accountId\": 1,\n  \"symbol\": \"AAPL\",\n  \"side\": \"BUY\",\n  \"quantity\": 5,\n  \"price\": 340.00,\n  \"idempotencyKey\": \"bruno-demo-order-001\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://10.8.78.168:8085/api/v1/orders",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": ["10", "8", "78", "168"],
              "port": "8085",
              "path": ["api", "v1", "orders"]
            },
            "description": "Returns immediately with status NEW — the fill/reject decision happens asynchronously in the executor. Check 'Get Order History' a moment later to see it resolve.\n\nidempotencyKey is a fixed literal (\"bruno-demo-order-001\") — change it before re-running, or you'll get 409 ORD-409 instead of a fresh order."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Cancel Order",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN>" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://10.8.78.168:8085/api/v1/orders/REPLACE_WITH_ORDER_UUID",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": ["10", "8", "78", "168"],
              "port": "8085",
              "path": ["api", "v1", "orders", "REPLACE_WITH_ORDER_UUID"]
            },
            "description": "Only succeeds while the order is still NEW. Replace REPLACE_WITH_ORDER_UUID in the URL with a real order's public UUID (the orderId field from a Place Order response, without the ORD- prefix) before sending — there's no auto-capture here."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Account",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN>" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://10.8.78.168:8085/api/v1/accounts/1",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": ["10", "8", "78", "168"],
              "port": "8085",
              "path": ["api", "v1", "accounts", "1"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Balance",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN>" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://10.8.78.168:8085/api/v1/accounts/1/balance",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": ["10", "8", "78", "168"],
              "port": "8085",
              "path": ["api", "v1", "accounts", "1", "balance"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Positions",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN>" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://10.8.78.168:8085/api/v1/accounts/1/positions",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": ["10", "8", "78", "168"],
              "port": "8085",
              "path": ["api", "v1", "accounts", "1", "positions"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Order History (all)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN>" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://10.8.78.168:8085/api/v1/accounts/1/orders",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": ["10", "8", "78", "168"],
              "port": "8085",
              "path": ["api", "v1", "accounts", "1", "orders"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Order History (filtered — status/from/to)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN>" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://10.8.78.168:8085/api/v1/accounts/1/orders?status=FILLED&from=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-12-31T23:59:59Z",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": ["10", "8", "78", "168"],
              "port": "8085",
              "path": ["api", "v1", "accounts", "1", "orders"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "status", "value": "FILLED", "description": "One of NEW, FILLED, CANCELLED, REJECTED — optional." },
                { "key": "from", "value": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z", "description": "ISO-8601 instant — optional." },
                { "key": "to", "value": "2026-12-31T23:59:59Z", "description": "ISO-8601 instant — optional." }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Trade API — error catalogue examples",
      "description": "One request per entry in GlobalExceptionHandler.java's error envelope — {\"errorCode\":..., \"message\":...}. Each is set up to deliberately trigger that specific error.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "VAL-422 — validation failure (missing required field)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN>" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"accountId\": 1,\n  \"symbol\": \"AAPL\",\n  \"side\": \"BUY\",\n  \"quantity\": 5\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://10.8.78.168:8085/api/v1/orders",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": ["10", "8", "78", "168"],
              "port": "8085",
              "path": ["api", "v1", "orders"]
            },
            "description": "price and idempotencyKey both missing — 422 VAL-422."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "ACC-403 — suspended account",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN>" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"accountId\": 2,\n  \"symbol\": \"AAPL\",\n  \"side\": \"BUY\",\n  \"quantity\": 1,\n  \"price\": 340.00,\n  \"idempotencyKey\": \"bruno-suspended-demo-001\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://10.8.78.168:8085/api/v1/orders",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": ["10", "8", "78", "168"],
              "port": "8085",
              "path": ["api", "v1", "orders"]
            },
            "description": "Uses the account-2 token (minted with accountId claim 2, matching the request body) so this genuinely exercises 'token reaches the account, but the account itself is SUSPENDED' (seed account ACC-10002) — 403 ACC-403 — rather than 'token doesn't reach this account at all' (a different code path, same response)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "INS-404 — unknown symbol",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN>" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"accountId\": 1,\n  \"symbol\": \"NOSUCHSYMBOL\",\n  \"side\": \"BUY\",\n  \"quantity\": 1,\n  \"price\": 340.00,\n  \"idempotencyKey\": \"bruno-unknown-symbol-001\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://10.8.78.168:8085/api/v1/orders",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": ["10", "8", "78", "168"],
              "port": "8085",
              "path": ["api", "v1", "orders"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "ORD-400 — insufficient funds",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN>" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"accountId\": 1,\n  \"symbol\": \"AAPL\",\n  \"side\": \"BUY\",\n  \"quantity\": 100000,\n  \"price\": 340.00,\n  \"idempotencyKey\": \"bruno-insufficient-funds-001\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://10.8.78.168:8085/api/v1/orders",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": ["10", "8", "78", "168"],
              "port": "8085",
              "path": ["api", "v1", "orders"]
            },
            "description": "100,000 shares at 340.00 vastly exceeds the seed account's cash balance — 400 ORD-400."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "ORD-409 (1/2) — first request with a fixed idempotency key (expect 200)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN>" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"accountId\": 1,\n  \"symbol\": \"AAPL\",\n  \"side\": \"BUY\",\n  \"quantity\": 1,\n  \"price\": 340.00,\n  \"idempotencyKey\": \"bruno-dup-demo-key-001\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://10.8.78.168:8085/api/v1/orders",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": ["10", "8", "78", "168"],
              "port": "8085",
              "path": ["api", "v1", "orders"]
            },
            "description": "Uses a fixed idempotency key on purpose, so the next request collides with it. Run this one first."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "ORD-409 (2/2) — same idempotency key again (expect 409)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN>" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"accountId\": 1,\n  \"symbol\": \"AAPL\",\n  \"side\": \"BUY\",\n  \"quantity\": 1,\n  \"price\": 340.00,\n  \"idempotencyKey\": \"bruno-dup-demo-key-001\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://10.8.78.168:8085/api/v1/orders",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": ["10", "8", "78", "168"],
              "port": "8085",
              "path": ["api", "v1", "orders"]
            },
            "description": "Identical body to (1/2), same idempotencyKey — the DB's unique constraint on orders.idempotency_key rejects this as 409 ORD-409 'Duplicate order'. Re-running the pair again needs a new idempotencyKey typed into both requests, since it's a fixed literal now."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Fauxnance API",
      "description": "The live external market-data sandbox the executor calls (executor/.../fauxnance/FauxnanceHttpClient.java). Auth is a plain X-Api-Key header, not the JWT used above.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get single quote",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "X-Api-Key", "value": "fnx_dev_2ntkvkZIUUuUKXTquhwnQwu26cTB2dLX" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://y4t9nq2bqf.execute-api.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/v1/quotes/AAPL",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": ["y4t9nq2bqf", "execute-api", "eu-west-2", "amazonaws", "com"],
              "path": ["v1", "quotes", "AAPL"]
            },
            "description": "What ExecutionService calls, once per order, to price it. Response has bid/ask/price — FillRule settles a BUY at ask, a SELL at bid."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get batch quotes (what the market-data poller calls)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "X-Api-Key", "value": "fnx_dev_2ntkvkZIUUuUKXTquhwnQwu26cTB2dLX" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://y4t9nq2bqf.execute-api.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/v1/quotes?symbols=AAPL,MSFT,GOOGL",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": ["y4t9nq2bqf", "execute-api", "eu-west-2", "amazonaws", "com"],
              "path": ["v1", "quotes"],
              "query": [{ "key": "symbols", "value": "AAPL,MSFT,GOOGL" }]
            },
            "description": "Up to 25 symbols per call — the quota-relevant HTTP request. The poller publishes one Kafka message per symbol from this single response, never one message per batch."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get remaining daily quota",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "X-Api-Key", "value": "xxx" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://y4t9nq2bqf.execute-api.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/v1/usage",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": ["y4t9nq2bqf", "execute-api", "eu-west-2", "amazonaws", "com"],
              "path": ["v1", "usage"]
            },
            "description": "2000 requests/day per key, resets 00:00 UTC."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
